# A number followed by an unknown unit names the valid units.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where duration > 1x
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..29
  PIPELINE@0..28
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..28
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..28
        NAME_REF@15..23
          IDENT@15..23 "duration"
        WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
        GT@24..25 ">"
        WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
        LITERAL@26..28
          TIMESPAN@26..28 "1x"
  WHITESPACE@28..29 "\n"

error[DS0003]: unknown timespan unit `x`
  --> query:1:28
  |
1 | from t | where duration > 1x
  |                            ^ not a timespan unit
  |
  = help: valid units are `d`, `h`, `m` (minutes), `s`, `ms`, `us` (or `µs`) and `tick` (100 ns)
